# Security & Testing

## Security checklist

Authn, authz, input validation, rate limits, CORS/CSRF, secure cookies, file/MIME validation, upload limits, injection/XSS defenses, secrets hygiene. Never trust user input, filenames, or client-side permissions.

## Env

No hard-coded secrets. Maintain `.env.example` without real credentials. Never commit `.env` with secrets.

## Docker

Use existing Docker for Postgres, MinIO, API, portal. Do not replace compose without need.

## Testing (minimum for important features)

Survey CRUD + authz, RBAC, Excel validation/duplicates/import, payment create/callback/idempotency/requery/refund, offline payment. Add E2E for critical journeys.

## Type safety

Avoid `any`. Prefer Zod/DTOs/enums/discriminated unions. Fix types — do not cast around errors.

## No production mocks

No fake APIs, fake payments, fake dashboards, hard-coded surveys, or fake auth in production paths. Mocks only in tests/dev.
